! mcp_bootstrap_p107.strap -- MCP, printed page 107:
! "***** EXIT CODES TO ERROR ROUTINE *****".
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.114, header READ not assumed: the
! top line prints "TIME CLOCK 00054041  PUNID 11011MCP  CARD ID
! CC000001  DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER 107".
!
! THIRTY-SIX LINES, AND THE COUNT WAS CONFIRMED, NOT ESTIMATED.  The
! rightmost column prints the card serial: line 1 is CC000001 and
! line 36 is CC000036, so line N is serial CC0000NN with no break,
! and CC000036 is the last printed row -- the rest of the page is
! blank.  Nothing fell off the top or the bottom of the render (the
! whole body was read in one 300-dpi frame, x=640 y=350 w=4300
! h=2900, and the blank lower half of the form is visible in it).
!
! >>> THE WHOLE PAGE IS DEFINITIONS, AND IT COMPILES NOT ONE BIT. <<<
! Lines 1-3 are the asterisk box around the heading.  Lines 4-25 and
! 29-36 are THIRTY SYN cards.  Lines 26, 27 and 28 are comment cards
! ("-", "-  *****   ERRORS IN MCP ONLY   *****", "-").  A SYN
! deposits no storage word, so this deck's entire check surface is
! THIRTY SYMBOLS AND ZERO LISTING ROWS -- the convention printed
! pp.24, 98, 99 and 101 established.  The BINARY OUTPUT column prints
! "+00000000" and the data-description column prints "NULL" on all
! thirty rows; that is the column working correctly on a definitions
! page and it must NOT be faked into a !CHECK.
!
! WHAT THE PAGE IS.  These are the error-exit codes MCP's error
! routine is entered with.  Each card is a SYN whose VALUE is a
! hexadecimal literal -- "SYN,(16)1001.0" -- with NO data
! description, which is why the data-description column prints NULL
! rather than p.101's "BU,nn ,10".  Lines 4-25 are the codes a
! problem program can provoke (printed -1 through -20 in the comment
! column); lines 29-36 are headed "ERRORS IN MCP ONLY" and print
! -75 through -82.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! >>> THERE IS NO SLC ON THIS PAGE, AND THIS DECK DOES NOT INVENT
! ONE. <<<
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Not one of the thirty-six lines carries an SLC, and not one row
! consumes storage, so the location counter neither moves nor is
! read here.  EVERY SYMBOL BELOW IS AN ABSOLUTE VALUE written into
! its own card, not an offset from a running counter: SIFERR is
! 0o10001.00 because the card says (16)1001, not because anything
! earlier in the assembly put the counter there.  The deck therefore
! carries NO SLC statement at all, and assembles from the default
! origin, and every !SYM still lands on the printed LOCATION.
!
! THAT IS A DELIBERATE DEPARTURE FROM p.101's DECK, WHICH CARRIES A
! NOT-PRINTED "SLC,(8)215000.0".  p.101 could justify it: printed
! p.99 line 11 set the counter to 215000.00 and pp.100-101 compile
! nothing, so the counter was still there.  THAT JUSTIFICATION DOES
! NOT SURVIVE TO HERE.  printed p.103 lays the communication region
! down at 215000.00..215021.00, so the counter is NOT at 215000 when
! this page begins, and I have not read pp.104, 105 or 106, so I do
! not know where it is.  Writing "SLC,(8)215000.0" here would assert
! something false, and it would assemble and pass, because nothing
! on this page depends on it.  Omitted instead, and recorded.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT ACTUALLY CHECKS WHAT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! * NO ROW IS AN INDEPENDENT BINARY CHECK, because there are no rows.
! * NO SYMBOL ON THIS PAGE IS REFERENCED BY ANY LANDED DECK.  A grep
!   of decks/, strap/ and tests/ for all thirty names returns
!   nothing (the single hit, SCWADR, is p.101's own control-word
!   address field in the UNIT AREA TABLE and is a different symbol).
!   So not one name here can fail a merge, and every !SYM below
!   rests on this page's own ink.
! * WHAT DOES CHECK THE DIGITS, ROW BY ROW, IS THAT THE STATEMENT
!   PRINTS THE VALUE IN HEX AND THE LOCATION COLUMN PRINTS THE SAME
!   VALUE IN OCTAL.  Two independent columns, twenty-eight rows:
!     (16)1001 = 0o10001   (16)1002 = 0o10002   (16)1003 = 0o10003
!     (16)1004 = 0o10004   (16)1005 = 0o10005   (16)1006 = 0o10006
!     (16)1007 = 0o10007   (16)1008 = 0o10010   (16)1009 = 0o10011
!     (16)010A = 0o00412   (16)0101 = 0o00401   (16)0102 = 0o00402
!     (16)0103 = 0o00403   (16)0104 = 0o00404   (16)0105 = 0o00405
!     (16)0106 = 0o00406   (16)0107 = 0o00407   (16)0108 = 0o00410
!     (16)0109 = 0o00411   (16)020A = 0o01012   (16)0705 = 0o03405
!     (16)0706 = 0o03406   (16)0707 = 0o03407   (16)0708 = 0o03410
!     (16)0709 = 0o03411   (16)080A = 0o04012   (16)0801 = 0o04001
!     (16)0802 = 0o04002
!   ALL TWENTY-EIGHT AGREE.  This is what pins the awkward glyphs:
!   the "A" in 010A/020A/080A is forced by the octal 412/1012/4012,
!   and the leading zeros of 0101..0109 are forced by 401..411.
!   THE REMAINING TWO ROWS ARE NOT HEX AT ALL -- line 7 is
!   "SUNNAV SYN,SCHNAV" and line 9 is "SUNNAS SYN,SIODI" -- and they
!   are checked instead by printing the SAME location as the symbol
!   they name (010003.00+ and 010004.00+).  Thirty names, twenty-
!   eight distinct addresses.
! * THE COMMENT COLUMN AGREES WITH THE HEX ON ALL THIRTY ROWS, and
!   this is recorded as a CHECK ON MY READING, NOT as a documented
!   encoding -- I have no primary source for it and am not inferring
!   one.  Observed: with the decimal code written as tens digit T
!   and units digit U, the hex is (T==0 -> 10, else 0T)(U==0 -> 0A,
!   else 0U).  -1 -> 1001, -9 -> 1009, -10 -> 010A, -19 -> 0109,
!   -20 -> 020A, -75 -> 0705, -80 -> 080A, -82 -> 0802.  Every one
!   of the twenty-eight hex rows fits, and lines 7 and 9 print the
!   codes (3, 4) of the symbols they SYN to.  As a check it is
!   strong; as semantics it is unsourced and is not claimed.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! A PRIMARY SOURCE CORROBORATES THE ENGLISH, AND THROUGH IT SEVEN
! SPELLINGS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! C22-6678-1, "IBM 7030 MCP Reference Manual" (June 1964), Appendix
! E "Messages to the Programmer", "Errors During Execution",
! printed p.54 = PDF p.54, lists "JOB ENDED, - ERROR TYPE YY" with
! YY = 01..23 and a sentence for each.  Error types 01-09 and 11-20
! line up with this page's comments one for one:
!
!   01 IF interrupt, instruction counter -.32 is not a B,$MCP
!   02 invalid pseudo-operation          03 channel not available
!   04 illegal IOD reference number      05 illegal PP I/O Table of
!      Exits on an IOD card              07 invalid Control word
!   08 invalid Control word address      09 communicate with
!      protected storage                 11 invalid exit address in
!      a $CHEX calling sequence          12 unit with an interrupt
!      stacked                           13 exceeded the limit of
!      maskable interrupts MCP will process
!   14 OP, AD, USA or DS interrupt while auto stacked
!   16 successful branch to location 32.0 or 32.32
!   17 illegal PTOE address in the refill field of $15
!   18 invalid FWA in a $COMM calling sequence
!   19 illegal instruction in a $FIXUP calling sequence
!   20 a $STLR when not in the Auto Stacked mode
!
! IT IS A LATER REVISION OF A DIFFERENT DOCUMENT AND IT DISAGREES IN
! PLACES -- its 06 is the Reel Pool Table and this page's -6 is
! "REQUEST FOR TOO MANY SCRATCH TAPES"; its 10 is a non-tape IOD in
! $ATID and this page's -10 is "DUMP FORMAT INVALID"; its 15 and 21
! are repeated UKs and this page's -15 is "BAD LABEL"; its codes
! 65-76 are interrupt classes and this page's -75..-82 are a
! separate "ERRORS IN MCP ONLY" group.  SO IT IS NOT USED AS
! VERIFICATION.  What it IS used for is the thing listing_oracle can
! never check, SPELLING, by confirming the ENGLISH WORDS the comment
! column abbreviates:
!   $COMM   (p.54 error 18)  -> the comment's "$CCMM" is $COMM, so
!           line 23's name is S C O M E R and not S C C M E R.
!   CHEX    (p.54 error 11)  -> line 16's "GOOF IN CHEX".
!   PTOE    (p.54 error 17)  -> line 22's name S P T O E X.
!   OR      (p.54 error 14, "OP, AD, USA, or DS") -> line 19's
!           comment prints "CR" and the word is OR; the name is
!           S O A U D.
!   $FIXUP  (p.54 error 19)  -> line 24.
!   $STLR   (p.54 error 20)  -> line 25.
!   "maskable interrupts MCP will process" (p.54 error 13) -> line
!           18's "50 MASKABLE INTERRUPTS" and the name STMMI.
!   "branch to location 32.0 or 32.32" (p.54 error 16) -> line 21's
!           "SUCCESSFUL B,$MCP", and decimal word 32 IS OCTAL 40, so
!           the name's last two cells are the DIGITS 4 and 0:
!           S B R 4 0.  (Measured: that round glyph is 87 px wide at
!           1200 dpi against 89 and 90 for the known O's in SNXOUT
!           and SOAUD, so WIDTH DOES NOT SEPARATE 0 FROM O on this
!           drum and the manual is what settles it.)
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE GLYPHS, AND THE ONE THAT IS NOT SETTLED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THIS PAGE OPENS ITS O's CONSTANTLY.  The octal LOCATION column
! prints 010001.00+ as "01CCC1.CC+" and 000412.00+ as "000412.CC+",
! and an octal field cannot hold a C, so those are 0's with
! certainty.  The same happens in letters: SFORBD prints "SFCRBD",
! SIODI prints "SICDI", SIOERR prints "SICERR", SPTOEX prints
! "SPTCEX", and in the comment column FOR prints "FCR", OR prints
! "CR", PTOE prints "PTCE" and $COMM prints "$CCMM".  SO AN OPEN
! ROUND GLYPH CARRIES ALMOST NO INFORMATION HERE.  Closed ones do:
! SNXOUT's O, SOAUD's O and SERCOD's O all print shut, and a shut
! glyph is never a damaged C.
!
! C vs D gave no trouble: every D on the page prints the straight
! vertical left stem and squared corners (SIODI, SFORBD, SOAUD,
! SERCOD, SCCWAD), against the stemless bowl of C and O.
! B vs 8 does not arise -- there is no hex byte column on this page.
!
! >>> THE UNRESOLVED ONE IS LINE 13's NAME, TRANSCRIBED SCCWAD. <<<
! Its comment is "- 8 CW ADDRESS INVALID" and C22-6678-1 p.54's
! error 08 is "invalid Control word address", so the English is CW
! AD and the obvious name would be the five-character SCWAD.  IT IS
! NOT FIVE CHARACTERS.  The name column's cell pitch was measured at
! 1200 dpi off eleven rows: the cells start at x = 134, 251, 368,
! 489, 611, 729 on every name, and line 13 has INK IN ALL SIX,
! exactly where line 12's SCWINV has its six.  So SCWAD is excluded
! ON GEOMETRY, not on ink -- the comment column is an oracle for
! WHICH LETTER a glyph is, and it cannot delete a cell.  The six
! cells read S, round, round, W, A, D, and since both round glyphs
! are open neither is decidable by shape.  The surviving candidates
! are SCCWAD, SCOWAD and SOCWAD; SCCWAD is transcribed because it is
! the only one that reads as English (CCW ADdress).  IT RESTS ON INK
! ALONE: nothing references it, and listing_oracle checks LOCATIONS
! and BINARY and never spellings, so this is a name that can be
! wrong and still pass everything.  DO NOT "FIX" IT TO SCWAD -- that
! would be deleting a printed character to match a guess.
!
! SETTLED BY THE SAME RULE, THE OTHER WAY: line 23 prints the same
! S-round-round shape and IS reduced to five letters plus one,
! SCOMER, because there the comment supplies the word ($COMM) and
! the reduction is a LETTER substitution (C -> O in cell 3), not a
! deleted cell.  Printed form "SCCMER"; transcribed SCOMER.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! CONVENTIONS AND OMISSIONS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (1) BLANKS INSIDE SYMBOL NAMES ARE DROPPED, as on every page since
!     p.2.  Only two names here print with an interior blank --
!     line 24's "S FIXP" and line 36's "S ASNER" -- and they become
!     SFIXP and SASNER.  Line 25's SERCOD is printed one cell to the
!     RIGHT of every other name (its cells start at 245, not 134);
!     that is the card column the name was punched in and it is not
!     a leading blank in the symbol.
! (2) THE STATEMENTS ARE WRITTEN EXACTLY AS PRINTED, "SYN,(16)1001.0"
!     -- SYN with NO data description and a hexadecimal value.  The
!     trailing ".0" is the bit offset and is kept.
! (3) LINES 1, 2, 3, 26, 27 AND 28 COMPILE NOTHING AND ARE NOT
!     TRANSCRIBED.  1 and 3 are asterisk rules, 2 is the heading
!     "-*****   EXIT CODES TO ERROR ROUTINE   *****", 26 and 28 are
!     bare "-" cards and 27 is "-  *****   ERRORS IN MCP ONLY
!     *****".  All six print an empty LOCATION and an empty BINARY
!     OUTPUT.
! (4) THE LOCATIONS ARE NOT MONOTONIC AND THAT IS NOT A MISREAD:
!     010001 .. 010011, then 000412, then 000401 .. 000411, then
!     001012, then 003405 .. 003411, then 004012, 004001, 004002.
!     A SYN does not advance the location counter, so the cards are
!     in card order and the addresses are in whatever order the
!     codes fall.  Lines 6/7 and 8/9 print the SAME location twice
!     for two different names, which is what SYN,symbol does.
! (5) EVERY LOCATION PRINTS A TRAILING "+" -- the sign, printed as a
!     suffix the way printed p.84's negative SYN prints
!     "000001.00-".  All thirty.  It is dropped in the !SYM lines
!     below because listing_oracle's loc_bits parses "word.bit" and
!     has no sign field, which is what pp.99 and 101 do.
! (6) EVERY ONE of the thirty-six line numbers carries an asterisk
!     right after it ("4*", "36*"), exactly as pp.99 and 101 do.
!     That is the line-number column and not the mark that sits
!     after a LOCATION on pp.3/37/88/97/98.  No location on this
!     page carries a mark.
! (7) NOTHING ELSE.  No printed spelling on this page was refused by
!     strap_asm; there is no substitution anywhere in this deck.
!     The hexadecimal literal "(16)nnnn.0", the data-description-
!     less "SYN,value" and "SYN,symbol" all assemble as printed.
! (8) TAIL SCOPE: pp.99+ are outside the TAIL,(2)G block that p.2
!     opened and p.98 line 37 closed with UNTAIL,(2), so a name here
!     may legitimately repeat a name from pp.2-98 at a different
!     address.  None of these thirty does, as it happens -- the grep
!     above found no collision -- but the rule is recorded.

! ---- ***** EXIT CODES TO ERROR ROUTINE ***** (lines 1-3) ---------
SIFERR  SYN,(16)1001.0              ! line  4 - 1 ILLEGAL IF
                                     !            INTERRUPT
SOPCI   SYN,(16)1002.0              ! line  5 - 2 PSEUDO CP CODE
                                     !            INVALID
SCHNAV  SYN,(16)1003.0              ! line  6 - 3 CHANNEL NOT
                                     !            AVAILABLE
SUNNAV  SYN,SCHNAV                  ! line  7 - 3 UNIT NOT AVAILABLE
SIODI   SYN,(16)1004.0              ! line  8 - 4 PHONY IOD
SUNNAS  SYN,SIODI                   ! line  9 - 4 UNIT NOT ASSIGNED
SPPTNG  SYN,(16)1005.0              ! line 10 - 5 ILLEGAL PP T.O.E.
                                     !            ON IOD CARD
S2BIG   SYN,(16)1006.0              ! line 11 - 6 REQUEST FOR TOO
                                     !            MANY SCRATCH TAPES
SCWINV  SYN,(16)1007.0              ! line 12 - 7 CW INVALID
SCCWAD  SYN,(16)1008.0              ! line 13 - 8 CW ADDRESS INVALID
                                     !   (six printed cells; see the
                                     !   glyph note above)
SFORBD  SYN,(16)1009.0              ! line 14 - 9 COMMUNICATION WITH
                                     !            PROTECTED AREA
SFORMT  SYN,(16)010A.0              ! line 15 -10 DUMP FORMAT INVALID
SNXOUT  SYN,(16)0101.0              ! line 16 -11 GOOF IN CHEX
SUSUPP  SYN,(16)0102.0              ! line 17 -12 UNIT SUPPRESSED
STMMI   SYN,(16)0103.0              ! line 18 -13 50 MASKABLE
                                     !            INTERRUPTS
SOAUD   SYN,(16)0104.0              ! line 19 -14 OP,AD,USA OR DS
SLABNG  SYN,(16)0105.0              ! line 20 -15 BAD LABEL
SBR40   SYN,(16)0106.0              ! line 21 -16 SUCCESSFUL B,$MCP
SPTOEX  SYN,(16)0107.0              ! line 22 -17 BAD PTOE ADDRESS
SCOMER  SYN,(16)0108.0              ! line 23 -18 ILLEGAL $COMM FWA
                                     !   (printed "SCCMER"/"$CCMM")
SFIXP   SYN,(16)0109.0              ! line 24 -19 ILLEGAL FIXUP WD
                                     !            FOR $FIXUP
SERCOD  SYN,(16)020A.0              ! line 25 -20 PP BUFFER OUT OF
                                     !            BOUNDS FOR
                                     !            $STLR/$FHLR

! ---- *****   ERRORS IN MCP ONLY   ***** (lines 26-28) ------------
SIOERR  SYN,(16)0705.0              ! line 29 -75 MCP SETUP I/O ERROR
SREJ    SYN,(16)0706.0              ! line 30 -76 I/O OPERATION
                                     !            REJECTED
SQERR   SYN,(16)0707.0              ! line 31 -77 FILE NOT STACKED IN
                                     !            INT. QUE
SQ2BIG  SYN,(16)0708.0              ! line 32 -78 INTERRUPT QUE TOO
                                     !            SMALL
SPQFUL  SYN,(16)0709.0              ! line 33 -79 PRIME QUE TOO SMALL
SIFAS   SYN,(16)080A.0              ! line 34 -80 MCP ERROR WHILE
                                     !            AUTO STACKED
SEPGK   SYN,(16)0801.0              ! line 35 -81 MCP EPGK
SASNER  SYN,(16)0802.0              ! line 36 -82 SPECIAL ASSIGNMENT
                                     !            ERROR

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PRINTED LISTING -- all thirty definition lines, with the
! LOCATION, the BINARY OUTPUT and the data description exactly as
! printed.  The NAME column is given in its PRINTED form, which is
! not always the transcribed form (see lines 13 and 23).
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   line  4  010001.00+  +00000000  NULL  SIFERR  SYN,(16)1001.0
!   line  5  010002.00+  +00000000  NULL  SOPCI   SYN,(16)1002.0
!   line  6  010003.00+  +00000000  NULL  SCHNAV  SYN,(16)1003.0
